{
  "origin": "The third tier is the one that has to end the session, and on a feature it has no epic machinery to lean on: the concern is written and delivered straight to the source discussion's queue, the work is committed, and the session stops dead — no Step 8, no conclude gate, nothing that would let a later turn carry on building against a record that has just been reopened. It is also the one arm the block gate reaches without a pick: the gate offers the fork's sides numbered with the recommendation first and **Comment**, and this walk takes the Comment — the user saying the question changes what cancelling an order means and is not theirs to settle alone. It pins the terminal stop and what the delivery leaves behind — the discussion reopened, its queue holding one concern, the specification flagged to reconcile and its source row staled — because every one of those is what the way back is built from, and a walk that instead marched on to the conclude gate would look successful while doing exactly what the tier exists to prevent.",
